IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `psa93-types`
IMPORT `psa93-leavers`

-- Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK) — GOAL 2: CASH EQUIVALENT TRANSFERS (ss 93A,
-- 94, 95(1A), 98, 99).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1993-48.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — cash equivalent transfers`

-- s 95(1A) "In the case of a right acquired under section 94(1), the
-- application must be made— (a) within the period of 3 months beginning with
-- the guarantee date ..., and (b) if the cash equivalent relates to benefits
-- that are not flexible benefits, by no later than the date that falls one
-- year before the member attains normal pension age." NOTHING for money
-- purchase rights (s 94(2)), which have no s 95(1A) limit.
@ref ss 94, 95(1A)
@export The last day for a member to apply to take a cash equivalent shown in a statement of entitlement under s 95(1A) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): the end of the 3 months beginning with the guarantee date, or, for benefits that are not flexible, one year before normal pension age if that is earlier; NOTHING for money purchase rights under s 94(2). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`    @desc The date the member reaches normal pension age
      t IS A `Transfer facts`  @desc The kind of benefits and the guarantee date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to apply for a transfer for` l `with` t MEANS
    IF   t's `money purchase benefits`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (IF   t's `flexible benefits`
               THEN threeMonths
               ELSE `the earlier of` threeMonths (`add months` (l's `reaches normal pension age on`) (0 MINUS 12)))
    WHERE
        threeMonths MEANS `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` (t's `guarantee date`)

-- s 98(1): the right under s 94(1) is lost "if no application ... is made
-- within the period required by section 95(1A)".
@ref s 98(1)
@export Whether a member has lost the right to take a cash equivalent under s 98(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): a right from a statement of entitlement where no application was made within the s 95(1A) period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Leaver facts`, t IS A `Transfer facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer right is lost for` l `with` t IF
    CONSIDER `the last day to apply for a transfer for` l `with` t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
        CONSIDER t's `application made on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST a  THEN a GREATER THAN last

-- s 99(2): the trustees must carry out the transfer "(a) [for benefits other
-- than money purchase] within 6 months beginning with the guarantee date
-- ..., (b) [money purchase] within 6 months beginning with the date of the
-- application". (3): where forfeiture proceedings are pending and that date
-- is earlier than "the end of the period of 3 months after the conclusion" of
-- them, "before the end of that period of 3 months".
@ref s 99(2)-(3)
@export The last day for the trustees to carry out a transfer under s 99 of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): 6 months beginning with the guarantee date (benefits other than money purchase) or with the application date (money purchase), or, if later, 3 months after the conclusion of proceedings that may lead to forfeiture; NOTHING if no application was made. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Transfer facts`  @desc The kind of benefits, the guarantee and application dates, and any forfeiture proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the trustees' last day to transfer for` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `application made on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        JUST (CONSIDER t's `forfeiture proceedings concluded on`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN base a
              WHEN JUST c  THEN `the later of` (base a) (`add months` c 3))
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        base a MEANS
            IF   t's `money purchase benefits`
            THEN `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` a
            ELSE `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (t's `guarantee date`)

-- s 99(7): if the trustees "have not done what is needed ... within six
-- months of the date mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (2)",
-- they must notify the Regulatory Authority. "Within six months of the
-- date" is read like s 99(2)'s "6 months beginning with" it (changed after
-- the independent pass, T27, T29).
@ref s 99(7)
@export Whether the trustees must notify the Pensions Regulator under s 99(7) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK): an application was made and the transfer was not carried out within the six months beginning with the guarantee date (benefits other than money purchase) or the application date (money purchase), or has not been carried out. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Transfer facts`  @desc The kind of benefits, the guarantee and application dates, and when the transfer was carried out
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustees must notify the Regulator for` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `application made on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER t's `carried out on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST done THEN done GREATER THAN `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (start a)
    WHERE
        GIVEN a IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        start a MEANS IF t's `money purchase benefits` THEN a ELSE t's `guarantee date`
